  "prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress was established in January 2019 with the purpose of investigating and making recommendations on modernizing the operations of the House of Representatives. The committee, which is composed of an equal number of Democrats and Republicans, was created under H.Res. 6 and has the authority to hold public hearings and develop recommendations. The committee is focused on areas such as rules and procedures, leadership development, staffing, administrative efficiencies, technology, and the work of the House Commission on Congressional Mailing Standards. The committee has been provided with funding and can use House staff services. The committee's first hearing was held in March 2019, and subsequent hearings have included testimony from Members and outside experts on various proposals for improving congressional operations. The committee is required to submit a final report to the House, which will include findings and policy recommendations, and must meet a higher threshold of two-thirds of the committee to publish the report. The committee's work is subject to House rules regarding the availability of proceedings and documents to the public.",
  "scored_prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress was established in January 2019 with the purpose of investigating and making recommendations on modernizing the operations of the House of Representatives. The committee, which is composed of an equal number of Democrats and Republicans, was created under H.Res. 6 and has the authority to hold public hearings and develop recommendations. The committee is focused on areas such as rules and procedures, leadership development, staffing, administrative efficiencies, technology, and the work of the House Commission on Congressional Mailing Standards. The committee has been provided with funding and can use House staff services. The committee's first hearing was held in March 2019, and subsequent hearings have included testimony from Members and outside experts on various proposals for improving congressional operations. The committee is required to submit a final report to the House, which will include findings and policy recommendations, and must meet a higher threshold of two-thirds of the committee to publish the report. The committee's work is subject to House rules regarding the availability of proceedings and documents to the public.",
  "score": 34.71074330578514,
  "answers": [
    "On January 4, 2019, the House established the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress by adopting Title II of H.Res. 6, the House rules package for the 116th Congress (2019-2020), on a 418-12 vote. The purpose of the select committee as stated in its authorizing resolution is \"to investigate, study, make findings, hold public hearings, and develop recommendations on modernizing Congress.\" Twelve Members, six from each party, have been selected by their leadership to serve on the select committee during its year-long investigation. The committee's authorizing resolution requires its membership to include two Members from the freshman class of the 116th Congress, two Members of the Rules Committee, and two Members of the Committee on House Administration. Funding for the select committee in the amount of $487,500 was provided through House adoption of H.Res. 245 on March 27, 2019. The committee has held four hearings to date, with additional meetings likely. Committee operations are scheduled to end on February 1, 2020. Any final report of the committee will be made public. Publication of the final report will require approval from at least two-thirds of the committee. Given that both parties are equally represented on the committee, some amount of bipartisan support will be needed to approve and publish the final report."
  ],
